LINEAGE OF THE RISK METRIC
--------------------------

`samples/risk-metric.pine` and `packages/core/src/indicator/` are this
project's own work and are covered by the grant above. Where the idea came
from is worth stating anyway, because it did not come from nowhere.

    Oakley Wood's "Risk Metric" (© Oakley Wood 2021) is a short TradingView
    indicator. It plots (close − 1460-day SMA) / 1460-day standard deviation,
    normalised by −35.64·ln(t) + 1008.1, against four flat reference lines —
    about twenty lines in total.

    `riskOne` here follows that idea with its own refitted coefficients
    (−38.12·ln(t) + 1078.5). Nothing else in this project is in his script:
    not the second or third sub-metric, not the averaging of the three, and
    not the strategy layer — the latched DCA entries, the tiered exits, the
    position sizing or the trading window.

    Metric 2 follows an idea of Ben Cowen's. Metric 3 follows Ben Cowen and
    the TradingView user "wugamlo", whose 50DMA/50WMA script is linked from
    the source. Metric 1's approach is credited in the source to "Andy".

    A formula is an idea rather than an expression, and none of these were
    transcribed. The acknowledgement above is a courtesy, and the right one to
    pay.

    An earlier version of this file said the opposite — that the Pine source
    was Oakley Wood's and the port derived from it — and blocked publishing
    this repository for months on that basis. It was wrong. The mistake was
    reading a bare `// Oakley Wood` header, which named the lineage rather
    than the author, as naming the author.


